# pnpm 11 reads only auth and registry settings from this file. The former
# `node-linker`, `auto-install-peers` and `strict-peer-dependencies` entries
# moved to `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, where pnpm 11 reads them. Do not add a
# non-registry setting here: pnpm ignores it in silence.

# Genesis publishes @genesis/* packages PUBLIC on npmjs.com (the default
# registry) — no per-consumer auth required. See docs/poc-plan.md and
# docs/research/publishing-setup.md for the pivot rationale (April 2026).
# Publishing uses NPM_TOKEN in CI; local dev needs no npm auth.
